# DijiOne Platform — environment contract
#
# Superseded by Phase 2.5. There is no longer one shared .env for a single
# app — each of the 8 services has its own .env.example in its own
# directory, since each is an independently deployable process with its
# own configuration:
#
#   apps/platform-api/.env.example
#   apps/admin-api/.env.example
#   apps/talent-api/.env.example
#   apps/birthday-api/.env.example
#   apps/spark-api/.env.example
#
# (shell-web/admin-web/talent-web need no .env — they call same-origin
# relative paths only; see docs/platform/service-contracts.md "Gateway /
# routing".)
#
# See docs/platform/local-development.md for full setup instructions and
# docs/platform/environment.md for the environment & secrets contract
# (what may and may not be committed).
# The values that matter most: JWT_DEV_SECRET and INTERNAL_SERVICE_SECRET
# must be IDENTICAL across every backend service's .env — they're the
# shared trust anchors the whole service split depends on (see
# docs/platform/service-contracts.md "Service-to-service trust
# boundaries").
